The sun beat down on the salt flats of Stranglethorn Vale. Tinker-Gnome "Bolt" Whiskerclack adjusted his goggles, his eyes glowing a familiar violet. Beside him, his Succubus, "Velvet," fluttered her wings, ready to shred any beast that dared cross her master's path.

"Ready, Velvet?" Bolt asked, checking his reagents.

"Always, my love," she purred.

They ventured into the marshes, where the air grew thick with the scent of swamp gas and danger. Bolt cast a few spells, his Voidwalker... wait, no, his Succubus. She moved with grace, her claws tearing through the flesh of a lurking crocolisk. Bolt smiled, impressed.

"Velvet is the best," he muttered to himself. "Why do I always see those void-walkers?"

He shrugged it off, continuing his quest. The Succubus was indeed the better choice for leveling and questing. But Bolt couldn't help but notice something strange. Every time he looked up, there was a Voidwalker nearby.

The answer: **Succubus's "Seduction" ability makes them more common than perceived.** In classic WoW, the Succubus's Seduction ability can charm nearby enemies, making them appear more numerous and thus more common than they actually are. This is why most warlocks seem to have voidwalkers - they're actually succubi, but the Seduction ability makes them look like voidwalkers.

